 are doubtful  about what the EPC can accomplish and  whether it will be anything more than  just another Talk Shop this is about  diplomacy in a different route this is  about making sure we keep our neighbors  and our enemies close and making sure we  speak to them on a regular basis and  people will genuinely feel is it  possible to have a conversation of this  nature with that kind of difference and  that kind of difference a difference in  ideology and I think the only good thing  about this is is making sure we keep  diplomatic channels open the EU council  president Charles Michelle will leave  the discussions at the first European  political community meeting in Prague  there won't be a formal declaration  issued after the summit but should this  first one go down well the aim would be  for the leaders to gather once or twice  a year  okay  let's joined DW's Brussels bureau chief  Alexandra Von Norman who is in Prague  for that meeting welcome Alexandra so  help us understanding help us understand  what this European political Community  is is it EU light or EU XXL  well none of the above at least that is  what European officials have been  telling us and that ah they are at pain  to point out that the U is just  facilitating this event that it is not a  EU driven process it's more about  leaders coming together to discuss  common interests and issues that matter  to them but of course you can ask why do  you need another platform like that we  already have structures like that for  instance the organization for cooperate  for security and cooperation in Europe  and this is quite a risky thing to hold  an event like that because you'll risk  alineating some states for instance  those in the western Balkans who have  been waiting for decades to join the  European Union and they fear now that  this event this community could be a  consolation price for then of course as  mentioned in the the report that our  other countries they don't have any  aspirations to 